# BruinWeb environment variables
#
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. The site builds and deploys with none of them
# set — the affected integration simply reports itself as unavailable rather
# than substituting invented data.
#
# None of these may be prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_. They are read only by
# build-time adapters running on the server, never by browser JavaScript, so no
# secret ever reaches the client bundle.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development, or add them in Vercel under
# Project → Settings → Environment Variables (Production + Preview).

# --- UCLA Lectures / Panopto (not yet implemented) ---------------------------
# All three are required together. With any of them missing, the Lectures
# section renders its clearly-labelled "Coming Soon" placeholder template.
# Obtain these from your institution's Panopto administrator (Panopto admin →
# System → API Clients, using the Client Credentials grant).

# Hostname of the Panopto site, without a scheme. Example: ucla.hosted.panopto.com
PANOPTO_SITE_HOST=

# OAuth2 client id issued by the Panopto administrator.
PANOPTO_CLIENT_ID=

# OAuth2 client secret. Never commit a real value.
PANOPTO_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Build behaviour ---------------------------------------------------------
# Set to 1 to bypass the on-disk HTTP cache and force fresh fetches.
BRUINWEB_DISABLE_CACHE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scheduled refresh (GitHub Actions secret — NOT a build variable)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The scheduled rebuild workflow needs a Vercel Deploy Hook URL. It is stored as
# a GitHub Actions repository secret named VERCEL_DEPLOY_HOOK_URL, never in this
# file and never in the repository: the URL is itself the credential, and anyone
# holding it can trigger deployments.
#
# Create it at: Vercel → Project → Settings → Git → Deploy Hooks
# Store it at:  GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions
#
# VERCEL_DEPLOY_HOOK_URL is intentionally absent from this file.
